{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481660-shadow-lords","id":1481660,"title":"Shadow lords","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-22T07:31:42-07:00","id":1481660,"title":"Shadow lords","content":"I recently have finished reading the Shadow lords revised tribebook and I liked it. They resemble in many ways the scorpion clan from Legend of the 5 rings, they are extremely loyal to Gaia, but also capable if any means to achieve their goals (exitus acta provat), even dealing and using the wyrm. As characters, they could be fertile ground to certain kind of problematic players, though. Their tendency to manipulate everyone and using even their packs is a narrative highway to hell, only appropriate to mature players and storytellers. What are your experiences with this tribe? Have you played them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T08:43:36-07:00","id":1481665,"title":"","content":"Oh boy, Shadow Lords do in fact attract players who don't know the difference between &quot;I do awful things for Gaia&quot; and &quot;I am playing Vampire in Werewolf and I want all the stuff!&quot;<br /> <br /> That has been a huge issue, which is why Shadow Lord players in online games are observed if they fall into the latter category.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the tribe, because they are one of the few who have done actual work to fix old mistakes. Look at the Lazarite Movement and especially the Children of Bat. This makes them a great opposite to the Silver Fangs, who barely have made any moves to admit they've effed up at all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T10:57:13-07:00","id":1481674,"title":"","content":"They are exactly like the Scorpion Clan of L5R, and like the Scorpions, they are played horribly by most of the players.<br /> Can't blame them tho', Palyers needs to be educated, its the GM's responsibility to teach players; this is why when I have a new player or a regular that tries out something new, I don't allow any &quot;seasoned&quot; character, his/hers first needs to start as human that will be embraced - to know what is it like to be &quot;groomed&quot; to be a Lasombra for example or Tzimisce or basically anything - and educated to the ways of the vampire Clan/bloodline during several private sessions before his character would be released in to a coteris/pack. Sure it would be easier to let hem do their homework, but lets face it, we all had our fair share of &quot;fishmalks&quot; amoung our players... heck even had such a character as newbies!<br /> Same goes for a Werewolf; start as a cub, before first change, to play out a little life as a member of a Shadow Lord family, be among kinfolks, then the First Change, then a few months traning with similar young cubs (if those cubs are other players not just NPCs, even better), to prepare for the Rite of Passage, and to be a young Shadow Lord, preferably under a mentor. <br /> A bit like the intro in the SL tribe book.<br /> There are clans and tribes. dharmas, kiths, Dynasites and Houses and so on that are not that easy to be played &quot;right&quot; (I know, this sounds harsh and extremly elitist, but who that is without this sin among you, let cast the first stone at me) and on the long run totally worth it to educate new players, even if it means several hours of extra/private time playing it out... but duh, we like to tell stories and like to play!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T18:43:03-07:00","id":1481708,"title":"","content":"I pretty much like all the tribes. As long as they provide enough concepts for STs and players while remaining true to their theme, I can use them in some fashion.<br /> <br /> I am not a big fan of any the Revised era sourcebooks because 1) they have a tendency to ignore the moral complexity and failings previously established in favor of a more black and white high fantasy metaplot, and 2) related to the first, they utterly ignore or retcon any prior canon that gets in the way of their new story to tell.<br /> <br /> Much of the extremely dubious dealings of the Shadow Lords were ignored. The secret society of the Masks is basically dismissed as irrelevant because of their new favorite Mary Sue NPC, the Margrave. Their &quot;fear is the path to power&quot; is just forgotten as a setting element. The Society of Nidhogg? Also completely eliminated once again by Margrave Mary Sue. The Lazarite Movement, which seemed an attempt by Shadow Lord metis to build their own personal power base among the Metis, also no longer exists. The Margrave is just that good of a leader!<br /> <br /> The Bringers of Light still exist, but curiously the book seems completely unconcerned about a camp whose main purpose is to justify Shadow Lords dealing with Wyrm minions. Despite repeating that many have fallen to the Wyrm, this doesn't seem to present any problems. Since the Bringers of Light philosophy is basically &quot;I'm going to prove I can't become an alcoholic by drinking as much as I can&quot;, I always took their claims with a big dose of salt. Now I always liked this camp because it was an easy way to justify a Garou working with vampires to some degree. That is a good NPC in both Vampire or Werewolf, as an ST can do lots of things with it.<br /> <br /> Then we have the Judges of Doom, the star chamber vigilantes of the Garou Nation. Justice among the Garou is essentially sept based. So a self selected group of Shadow Lords who decide to take legal matters into their own hands is a very big problem. It means they are extra-judicial killers. But the revised tribebook just ignores the moral problems by stating the Margrave supports them so it's OK. I wonder what the other tribes think about this? Because many tribes handle their justice pretty severely, I imagine the Judges probably kill mostly Bone Gnawers... so maybe the other tribes don't mind. Maybe the Children of Gaia do, but they are probably the tribe next in line for the Judges' killings.<br /> <br /> There are some other issues with the revised sourcebook as well. It has the Typhon totem there. Unfortunately, the original Typhon totem was introduced in Rage Across Russia where it is explicitly a defector totem to the Wyrm so it can gain more power and escape the harsh demands of Thunder's rule, and it is slowly corrupting the Shadow Lord packs and septs that have it as as their totem. This is completely ignored in Revised as if it never happened. Is this not brought up in the tribebook because it is oriented to players, and they don't want to spoil the truth? Or is it another case of the writers simply ignoring canon to present the tribe in a much better light? Probably the latter.<br /> <br /> Lastly, I have a complaint more about omission. No mention is made of the Hakaken cults among the Shadow Lords, which is a thing we know from the Book of the Wyrm. I always thought this was a fascinating concept especially because Hakaken was supposed to be one of the greatest Garou heroes ever before he foolishly danced the Labyrinth. The story of Hakaken and his lingering cults among the Shadow Lords are an intriguing concept. Lost opportunity here. But given the general white washing of the tribe here (which happened to every tribe during the Revised era), it's not a surprise this was ignored.<br /> <br /> In many ways, the Shadow Lords were intended as one of the designated bad guys in early Werewolf, so I welcome a more nuanced approach to the tribe that show its loyalty to Gaia and the Garou Nation. But Revised went way too far in the other direction. They either outright eliminated the more villainous camps in the tribe, or simply pretended problematic ones presented any issues at all. By doing so, they made the tribe much less interesting. As an ST, I can do a lot more using some of these secret societies and camps than I can with &quot;the Margrave is just so awesome and has taken care of all of these problems for you!&quot;. And as a player, the conspiratorial nature of the tribe is one of the reasons people like playing them. Getting ride of these secret conspiracies just makes the tribe more generic.<br /> <br /> It's perfectly OK for STs to disallow certain camps or concepts for PCs if it'll be too problematic for the game. But the wholesale elimination of them by an offscreen NPC, or ignoring them entirely, was not a good solution.<br /> <br /> The Shadow Lords were right proper bastards that you hoped would be on your side rather than against you, but you prepared accordingly. And I think that's how they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T19:22:57-07:00","id":1481712,"title":"","content":"I can't help but wonder if this &quot;Margrave&quot; was a player character in a test session? Because pulling off these sorts of miracles and being this noble sounds like something a player character would do over the course of a long campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-22T23:41:30-07:00","id":1481730,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I actually think the heroic tone works better for the Lords. Because if they were straight-up token bad guys of the tribes, a lot of the nuance they gained in the revised would be lost.<br /> <br /> Especially when you take them in the context of what they do to protect Gaia vs what they have accomplished. Shadow Lords are right bastards, they torture, tip-off vampires, maul, make deals with Wyrmy creatures and are extremely cutthroat among each other.<br /> <br /> Yet, it is -these- garou who have managed to do one of the bigger reparations to the Fera. Not the Glass Walkers, not the Bone Gnawers, not the Children of Gaia and very much not the Silver Fangs These manipulative, power-hungry, litany tap-dancing torturers, who have actually succeeded in part-way redeeming a Wyrm totem. Because they never make the same mistake twice.<br /> <br /> That to me creates a lovely question of ambiguity. What are the Lords doing that other tribes aren't? Why is it that brutality and manipulation have born fruit where compassion and kindness have not?<br /> <br /> (And I prefer that Children of the Bat are legit. Because if they were just covert Wyrm-tainted, it would rob the situation of its entire point.)<br /> <br /> Stuff like that is delicious moral ambiguity for me that I love to explore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-23T16:20:54-07:00","id":1481794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481660-shadow-lords?p=1481712#post1481712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't help but wonder if this &quot;Margrave&quot; was a player character in a test session? Because pulling off these sorts of miracles and being this noble sounds like something a player character would do over the course of a long campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's mainly just bad writing as the Revised era had a serious problem thinking that writing for RPGs was the same as writing a (bad) novel. But I don't discount the possibility that some of the signature characters were either someone's PC, an NPC they ran as ST, or an expy of such.<br /> <br /> My main problem with the Margrave is that when he's introduced, he's just this Superman who has accomplished all of these things. We're not shown anything about what he did to accomplish them, or the cost to do so. It seems he's just so awesome it happened. This guy never had any political rivals? No one was concerned about how he was stripping them of their power base? What kind of casualties did his supporters take while he was doing all of these things? How many enemies within the tribe did he have to kill? What affect is that going to have? The books just ignore these questions. At least I don't remember them being addressed. It's just bad writing because it's what's necessary to move the metaplot along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481660-shadow-lords?p=1481730#post1481730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> I actually think the heroic tone works better for the Lords. Because if they were straight-up token bad guys of the tribes, a lot of the nuance they gained in the revised would be lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind individual Shadow Lords being heroic. But the tribe itself can't be heroic or villainous. The tribe is just a collection of individuals. The individuals are heroic, villainous, noble, self-serving, etc. I think the game is better when each tribe has lots of individuals of different types. The Shadow Lords seem to be of a more high risk, high reward kind of tribe. So it's OK they have a lot of success and pull things off. But when things go wrong, they go very wrong - see Hakaken, Nightmaster, the followers of Typhon in Rage Across Russia, and the many crimes the tribe has committed over the millennia.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T01:43:14-07:00","id":1481834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1481660-shadow-lords?p=1481794#post1481794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind individual Shadow Lords being heroic. But the tribe itself can't be heroic or villainous. The tribe is just a collection of individuals. The individuals are heroic, villainous, noble, self-serving, etc. I think the game is better when each tribe has lots of individuals of different types. The Shadow Lords seem to be of a more high risk, high reward kind of tribe. So it's OK they have a lot of success and pull things off. But when things go wrong, they go very wrong - see Hakaken, Nightmaster, the followers of Typhon in Rage Across Russia, and the many crimes the tribe has committed over the millennia.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely. High risk and high reward is what I've told players about the Lords. What I like is that they have actually had successes, vs what other tribes have had.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}